From: Daniel Pawlik <pawlik.dan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: realtek: disable Pause advertising on RTL826x

RTL826x copper AN defaults to advertising Symmetric Pause (MMD 7.0x0010).
On hosts such as the Airoha AN7581 GDM4 path (Gemtek W1700K lan2), XFI
pause toward the PCS was already gated in the PCS driver, but copper
pause with the link partner still negotiates on and stalls PHY transmit
under upload load. That shows up as multi-tens-of-ms loaded latency on
upload while download stays fine. ethtool -A is not implemented on
airoha_eth, so the partner cannot keep pause forced off across reboot.

Clear Pause / Asym_Pause from phydev->supported in rtl826x_get_features()
so C45 AN never advertises them. Same 10G PHY IDs already disable EEE in
probe for related stability reasons.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Pawlik <pawlik.dan@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c	2026-09-29 12:16:18.612564108 +0200
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c	2026-09-29 12:16:18.651521331 +0200
@@ -2747,6 +2747,14 @@
 	linkmode_clear_bit(ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_10baseT_Full_BIT,
 			   phydev->supported);
 
+	/* Copper pause toward the link partner stalls TX under load on
+	 * USXGMII hosts that cannot drive ethtool pause ops (e.g. Airoha
+	 * GDM4). Keep Pause out of supported/advertising so AN never
+	 * enables it; XFI pause is handled separately in the PCS.
+	 */
+	linkmode_clear_bit(ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_Pause_BIT, phydev->supported);
+	linkmode_clear_bit(ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_Asym_Pause_BIT, phydev->supported);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
